<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n42895" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">scătĕ_bra</span></b> , ae,
			f.
		scateo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a bubbling</i> or <i>gushing up</i>
			of water (not ante-Aug., and very rare): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fontium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin. 5,
					1, 1, § 6</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fonticuli,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					31, 10, 46, § 108</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">(unda) scatebris arentia temperat arva,</span>”
				<i>spring - water</i>, <i>bubbling water</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					G. 1, 110</span></i>
			; cf. scaturex and scaturigines.</div>
